[test-suite name=test
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/test (spec/std-lib/test.md §6).

   Each program imports the bundled module via [?lib 'cx-stdlib/test']
   (resolver MUST be quoted) then calls [$test:fn args]. The LAST
   expression is the rendered result. String scalars render quoted;
   bool/int bare; null as `null`.

   RETURN POSTURE: every assertion, lifecycle hook, fail/skip and
   configure is declared `[returns null]` (§3). On the happy path the
   spec value is therefore the bare scalar `null`. A failing assertion
   raises CXER2200 (§5: "Any assertion failing"); the spec-grounded
   negative path is the bare error code.

   THUNKS: `$thunk::any` parameters (assert-throws, before-each,
   after-each, before-all, after-all) take a value. The spec-grounded
   thunk form is the v0.8.0 anonymous function literal [?fn () body]
   (spec/core/code.md §8.6) — a nullary [?fn] is a deferred computation.
   Lifecycle hooks register the thunk and return null without running it
   at registration time, so they are deterministic here.

   ASSERT-THROWS grounding: `fail` (§3.1) raises CXER2200 unconditionally.
   A thunk that calls [test/fail …] therefore raises CXER2200, which is a
   stable, spec-named code to assert the positive path against. A thunk
   that returns a value without raising drives the negative path
   (assert-throws itself raises CXER2200).

   EFFECTFUL / AMBIGUOUS: fixture-load is capability-gated (read, §8) and
   raises CXER0271 under the runner's deny-by-default capability set
   (AUTHORING.md "Capability-gated / effectful"). assert-snapshot,
   assert-shape (schema element grammar), assert-match (pattern element
   grammar), and fixture (tagged-sequence rendering) have an
   underspecified surface in test.md; their cases carry their best
   reading with a TODO(spec-ambiguous) line-comment and are listed in the
   report.

   NOTE: no inter-fixture comment blocks appear between cases except the
   TODO markers placed immediately above the case they annotate; all
   other explanatory prose lives in this doc header or in tags.
#]]

 [case id=test-001-assert-true level=core
  [tags test assert happy]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/test']
[$test:assert true]
#]]
  [out-text [#
null
#]]
 ]

 [case id=test-002-assert-false-fails level=core
  [tags test assert fail CXER2200]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/test']
[$test:assert false]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER2200
#]]
 ]

 [case id=test-003-assert-false-with-label-fails level=core
  [tags test assert label CXER2200]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/test']
[$test:assert false $label="round-trip"]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER2200
#]]
 ]

